  and production galaxy draw produced finite faint HDR (clear-air sampled peak 0.000602 nits).
  Applying the former grading equations with saved extra contrast 0.41573521 predicted exact
  black for every tested galaxy-only sample at exposure 0/1/2/4. This is a controlled diagnostic,
  not confirmation of live uniforms or the complete atmosphere/cloud/glare composition.
  Receipt: ../artifacts/galaxy-visibility-diagnostic.log.

  User approved the full replacement display path: scene-linear grading, filmic tone mapping
  and a cached 3D lookup. Implementation and validation are tracked in PBR.Postprocessing.md.
  This changes final scene presentation without changing celestial calibration or incident
  lighting. Positive grading no longer creates a fixed black cutoff, but the filmic toe,
  exposure bounds and display quantization still require the Phase 5 appearance checks.
  The 64-cube display lookup qualifies neutral-ramp error/channel difference within one SDR
  code. Actual generated 64-pixel galaxy/clear transmission/final RGBA8 checks at +4 and saved
  contrast retain 78 of 4096 pixels, at most one code; +2 retains one pixel. This is galaxy-only
  output, not a complete live sky. The user explicitly chose to retain standard filmic defaults
  and qualify night visibility separately. No toe, source-power or exposure-limit tuning is applied.
  Receipts and the complete contrast/exposure matrix are in PBR.Postprocessing.md.
  Fresh shader-enabled build and 113 focused grading/display/exposure/packed/runtime-handoff
  and shader-contract checks passed, with no skips or failures. Receipt:
